Toolchain runtime libraries
The fully static Linux executables contain libstdc++ and libgcc (GPL v3 or
later with the GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1, which permits distributing
binaries that statically incorporate the runtime without GPL obligations for
the rest of the program; https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gcc-exception-3.1.html)
and glibc (LGPL v2.1 or later, which permits static linking; source at
https://www.gnu.org/software/libc/). Windows executables statically link the
MinGW-w64 runtime and libstdc++/libgcc under the same runtime exception
(https://www.mingw-w64.org/). macOS executables use only system libraries.

lmcell does not include MaBoSS, PhysiBoSS, RoadRunner, or any other optional
PhysiCell addon. The serial OpenMP compatibility header in cpp/serial/omp.h
only supplies the two query functions used by the upstream serial build;
OpenMP pragmas are ignored by compilers when OpenMP is not enabled.

Integration modifications: the generated BioFVM build copy omits 13 premature
global-options vector writes in Microenvironment construction. The lmcell
wrapper explicitly initializes Cell_Definition::is_movable after copying.
Our expression compiler is adapted from lmnum/lmbio under the MIT license
